What is Linux User?
A user is an account that allows someone or a service to interact with a Linux system.

What is root?
root is the superuser account have all privileges.

uid - user ID
gid - group ID
Remember: UID 0 identifies the root superuser.

whoami - Check your current username
sudo adduser name - Create a new user
sudo deluser name - delete a user
id username - Verify the new user
cat /etc/passwd - List local user accounts
su - username - switch between Linux users
sudo groupadd groupname - Create the group
sudo groupdel groupname - delete the group
getent group groupname - verify 
sudo usermod -aG groupname username - Add a user to a group
sudo gpasswd -d groupname username - Remove a user from a group

